    "q-93906": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93906",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-8-3+4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
