    "q-93968": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93968",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =18-8-7 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
