    "q-140861": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140861",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 20\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
