    "q-140853": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140853",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
