      "dom_id": "step-q93684",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
