    "q-93997": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93997",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-5){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
