    "q-94045": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94045",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =(-4){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+\\,\\,3{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4$ and $b=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-4+3=-1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
