    },
    "q-94050": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94050",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$",
      "worked_solution": "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+1=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
